docs: universalize the project -- any vLLM model, any GPU host, generic disk names

Operator request: the repo must not be pinned to one specific deployment.
All prose now targets "any vLLM-served model on any NVIDIA GPU host";
MiMo-V2.6-Pro on 4x NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 is stated as the tested reference
example, not the primary/only target.

- OS mentions relaxed: "Debian host" -> "Linux host (any distribution)
  (tested on Debian 12)"; Python-version notes kept as distro-specific guidance.
- Hardware: "4x RTX PRO 6000" removed from all generic statements; TP4 hardware
  counts presented as a recommendation ("4+ GPUs recommended for TP4"), not a
  requirement. Architecture topology strings now say "TP4 or any parallelism,
  any served model".
- Runnable commands in README / docs / wiki now use generic placeholders
  ($HOME/models/<your-model-dir>, <your-org>/<your-model>) instead of
  hard-coded MiMo paths, so any model owner can copy-paste them.
- README x3 gained an "Add your own model" section (RU/ZH translations):
  copy configs/mimo-v2.6-pro to configs/<your-model>, fill identity.env
  geometry, run setup-identity.sh, and let each model get its own cache
  namespace. Explicitly notes that non-MiMo models are untested until a
  hardware run.
- Block-device naming stays generic (nvme0n1 / sda / vda) per the VM feedback.